# CNN Image Classification

This project uses **Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)** to classify chest X-ray images into different categories.

### 1. COVID-19 X-Ray Classification

The first part uses the **COVID-19 Radiography Dataset**, containing **COVID-19 and Normal chest X-ray images**. 
The dataset contains **3,616 COVID-19 images and 10,192 Normal images**. 
The images are preprocessed, augmented, and divided into training, validation, and testing datasets. 
A CNN model is trained to identify whether an X-ray belongs to the COVID-19 or Normal category.

### 2. Opacity X-Ray Classification

The second part applies the same CNN-based approach to a dataset containing **Normal and Opacity X-ray images**. 
The images are preprocessed and used to train and evaluate a binary image classification model.

### Overall

The project demonstrates the use of **deep learning and CNN for automated chest X-ray classification**, 
with model performance evaluated using accuracy and other classification metrics.
